  "id": "universal-design",
  "term": "universal design",
  "definition": "Universal design for learning is an inclusive educational framework used in policy and practice to support students, including those with intellectual disabilities, in accessing the general curriculum. In this context, its use is shaped by school systems and policies such as supervision, management, legal support, and funding.",
